CM_ SG_ 200 BMS_packSOC "This is the pack State of Charge";
CM_ SG_ 200 BMS_packVolt "This is the instantaneous total pack voltage value";
CM_ SG_ 200 BMS_packCurr "This is the current pack amperage value for the battery pack. This will report a constant 0 if no current sensor is selected";
CM_ SG_ 200 BMS_rollingCounter200 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 201 BMS_minPackVolt "This value is the mainimum pack voltage that the BMS is using to limit how low the pack voltage is allowed to be pulled down to";
CM_ SG_ 201 BMS_maxPackVolt "This value is the maximum pack voltage that the BMS is using to limit how high the pack voltage can be. This can be useful for communicating with chargers or charging stations expecting a maximum pack voltage value they are able to charge up to";
CM_ SG_ 201 BMS_packSummedVolt "This value is the sum of all the cells being monitored by the BMS and represents the overall pack voltage. It is essentially identical to the Pack Voltage value, except that it is reported wit ha higher resolution (0.01V versus 0.1V)";
CM_ SG_ 201 BMS_rollingCounter201 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 202 BMS_packResistance "This is the combined measured internal resistance for the entire battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 202 BMS_packAmphours "This is the calculated number of amphours remaining in the battery pack. This is used in part to calculate State of Charge";
CM_ SG_ 202 BMS_packSOH "This is the total state of health for the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 202 BMS_packDOD "This value represents the total pack depth of discharge (that is, the total percent of the battery that has been discharged to this point). This value does not account for any Drift";
CM_ SG_ 202 BMS_rollingCounter202 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_internalTemp "This signed value is the internal temperature measured by the BMS (specifically, it is the temperature of the heatsink case)";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_avgTemp "This signed value is the average temperature measured in the battery back by the thermistors";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_lowestThermistorID "This is the ID of the lowest temperature thermistor being sensed by the BMS. The lowest possible value is 1";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_lowestTemp "This signed value is the lowest temperature measured in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_highestThermistorID "This is the ID of the highest temperature thermistor being sensed by the BMS. The lowest possible value is 1";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_highestTemp "This signed value is the highest temperature measured in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 203 BMS_rollingCounter203 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 204 BMS_avgCellVolt "This is the voltage of the average measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 204 BMS_highCellVolt "This is the voltage of the highest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 204 BMS_lowCellVolt "This is the voltage of the lowest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 204 BMS_rollingCounter204 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 205 BMS_avgCellOpenVolt "This is the Open Voltage of the average measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 205 BMS_highCellOpenVolt "This is the Open Voltage of the highest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 205 BMS_lowCellOpenVolt "This is the Open Voltage of the lowest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 205 BMS_rollingCounter205 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 206 BMS_avgCellInternalResistance "This is the Internal Resistance of the average measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 206 BMS_highCellInternalResistance "This is the Internal Resistance of the highest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 206 BMS_lowCellInternalResistance "This is the Internal Resistance of the lowest measured cell in the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 206 BMS_rollingCounter206 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 207 BMS_pwrInputVolt "This is the voltage of the power source that directly powers the BMS (12v-24v nominal for the standard Orion BMS, 12v-48v nominal for the Orion JR BMS). NOTE: This value will read lower than the actual input voltage seen at the BMS due to internal diode voltage drop. This is normal and this value should not be used as a precise measurement";
CM_ SG_ 207 BMS_minCellVolt "This value is the minimum cell voltage that the BMS is using to limit how low individual cell voltages are allowed to be pulled down to";
CM_ SG_ 207 BMS_maxCellVolt "This value is the maximum cell voltage that the BMS is using to limit how high individual cell voltages can be. This can be useful for communicating with chargers or charging stations expecting a maximum cell voltage that they are able to charge up to";
CM_ SG_ 207 BMS_rollingCounter207 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_highCellResistanceID "This value is the ID of the highest cell resistance measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_lowCellResistanceID "This value is the ID of the lowest cell resistance measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_highCellOpenVoltID "This value is the ID of the highest cell open (sitting) voltage measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_lowCellOpenVoltID "This value is the ID of the lowest cell open (sitting) voltage measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_highCellVoltID "This value is the ID of the highest cell voltage measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_lowCellVoltID "This value is the ID of the lowest cell voltage measured by the BMS. The value is 1 based (valid range: 1-180)";
CM_ SG_ 208 BMS_rollingCounter208 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 209 BMS_totalPackADC "This is the raw voltage value from the total pack voltage sensor (NOT the sum of all the cell voltages). Only available on BMS models that support the separate total pack sensor";
CM_ SG_ 209 BMS_packChargeCurrLimkW "This is the pack Charge Current Limit expressed in kilowatts as opposed to amps";
CM_ SG_ 209 BMS_packChargeCurrLim "This is the pack Charge Current Limit. The value is, by default, reported as a positive value from 0 to whatever the maximum charge current limit is set to";
CM_ SG_ 209 BMS_rollingCounter209 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 210 BMS_packOpenVolt "This is the current total pack Open Voltage value";
CM_ SG_ 210 BMS_packDischargeCurrLimkW "This is the pack Discharge Current Limit expressed in kilowatts as opposed to amps";
CM_ SG_ 210 BMS_packDischargeCurrLim "This is the pack Discharge Current Limit. This value is, by default, reported as a positive value from 0 to whatever the maximum discharge current limit is set to";
CM_ SG_ 210 BMS_rollingCounter210 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 211 BMS_avgPackCurr "This is the AVERAGE current pack amperage value for the battery pack. This will report a constant 0 if no current sensor is selected. The average is taken over the last 1 second of operation so it will lag the instantaneous pack current value";
CM_ SG_ 211 BMS_maxPackCCL "This value is the programmed maximum continuous pack Charge Current Limit";
CM_ SG_ 211 BMS_maxPackDCL "This value is the programmed maximum continuous pack Discharge Current Limit";
CM_ SG_ 211 BMS_rollingCounter211 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 212 BMS_fanVolt "This is the raw voltage measured by the fan monitor circuit. This can be a maximum of 15V";
CM_ SG_ 212 BMS_adaptiveSOC "This is the calculated State of Charge value based on the Adaptive Total Capacity. As the BMS continues to learn more about the battery pack (specifically, how much capacity is actually in the pack versus how mush it is programmed to expect) this figure will become more accurate. It is expected for this value to differ, at least slightly, from the overall pack State of Charge parameter as that value is based on the programmed expected capacity, rather than the observed capacity";
CM_ SG_ 212 BMS_requestedFanSpeed "This is the current requested speed (0-6) of the battery fan";
CM_ SG_ 212 BMS_fanSpeed "This is the current speed (0-6) of the battery fan. The higher the speed, the faster the fan output should be";
CM_ SG_ 212 BMS_rollingCounter212 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 213 BMS_currLimStatus "This value is provided so the reasons for why a current limit either Charge Current Limit or Discharge Current Limit are being reduced by the BMS from the maximum allowable current. Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 213 BMS_adaptiveAmphours "This is the Pack Amphours value equivalent based on the Adaptive Total Capacity metric. This is NOT the total capacity of the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 213 BMS_adaptiveTotalCapacity "This is the total number of amphours that the BMS has 'observed' or learned during operation. Over time this will gradually be adjusted as the BMS continues to observe the battery pack";
CM_ SG_ 213 BMS_rollingCounter213 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 214 BMS_populatedCells "This represents the total number of populated (active) cells in the BMS. This can be equal or lower than the Max Cell Number";
CM_ SG_ 214 BMS_dtcStatus1 "This parameter contains the status of several BMS fault codes. Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 214 BMS_totalPackCycles "This is the total number of cycles that the battery pack has been put through since the BMS has started keeping track. On revision-D BMS units and newer this value is stored over complete power loss, though on earlier hardware revisions this value is lost when all power is cut to the BMS. A battery cycle is defined as a net transfer of the total Amphour capacity of the pack. In other words, on a 40 Ahr battery one cycle would be a net transfer of 40 Amphours";
CM_ SG_ 214 BMS_maxCellNumber "The maximum number of cells that the BMS is capable of supporting";
CM_ SG_ 214 BMS_rollingCounter214 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 215 BMS_dtcStatus2 "This parameter contains the status of several BMS fault codes. Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 215 BMS_failsafeStatus "Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 215 BMS_relayState "Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 215 BMS_rollingCounter215 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
CM_ SG_ 216 BMS_j1772ACVolt "This is the AC voltage that the BMS is using for internal calculations. This can be provided to the BMS by the charger if it supports this functionality (must be CANBUS enabled and able to transmit the AC voltage). Otherwise the BMS may assume a certain voltage based on the observed AC current limit";
CM_ SG_ 216 BMS_j1772ACPwrLim "This is the calculated AC power limit (expressed in watts) that the charger is allowed to consume";
CM_ SG_ 216 BMS_j1772ACCurrLim "This is the raw AC current limit being published by the J1772 compatible charging station";
CM_ SG_ 216 BMS_j1772PlugState "This represents the current status (state) of the J1772 inlet on the vehicle. Look at utility manual";
CM_ SG_ 216 BMS_rollingCounter216 "Increments once every 100ms (max value is 255 and rolls over). Can be used to ensure data is updating";
